# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ResumeMaxxer - frontend, production build
#
# Committed on purpose, unlike .env.local. Everything Vite exposes under the
# VITE_ prefix is compiled into the JavaScript bundle and is publicly readable,
# so this file may only ever hold PUBLIC values - and it holds no values at
# all, which is the point.
#
# Both are deliberately EMPTY, which means "same origin".
#
# The deployed app is one Vercel project with four services behind a single
# domain (see vercel.json), routed by path:
#
#     /api/auth/*   ->  auth service
#     /api/*        ->  FastAPI backend
#     /*            ->  this frontend
#
# So the API is reached at the relative path `/api/...` with no host at all.
# That is what makes the Better Auth session cookie first-party rather than
# cross-site, and it means there is no CORS preflight on any call.
#
# Setting either of these to a real host would undo that: the browser would go
# back to treating the auth cookie as third-party, which Safari and Chrome
# increasingly refuse to store.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

VITE_AUTH_URL=
VITE_API_URL=
